in @prism
in @meta
in @nl
in @glass
in @mirror/lens/cli

# @mirror/spec — the project manifold grammar.
#
# `mirror.spec` IS the multi-dimensional manifold kintsugi operates on
# (per docs/specs/mirror-spec-schema.md §1). Not a config file. Not a
# manifest. A typed prism declaration that names the project's sources,
# targets, altitudes, and settlement criteria. The substrate already
# has the vocabulary for shards, altitudes, and au; @mirror/spec lifts
# those into one top-level `project NAME { ... }` declaration per
# project.
#
# Consumer: @mirror/mosaic.focus reads a `mirror.spec` under this
# grammar to produce the build manifold (mosaic.mirror line 76:
# `focus(spec: ref) -> manifold { \ }`). This shard is what makes
# that focus parse.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/mirror-spec-schema.md §§3-7
# (source/legacy/target/cli/settle_on).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]].
# Related shards: lens/cli.mirror (the `target { cli { ... } }` consumer;
#                 the @mirror/lens family species post-migration),
#                 mosaic.mirror (the focus consumer),
#                 glass.mirror (transparency / au / property carriers).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/mirror/spec.mirror`
# declares `@mirror/spec` and only that.

# === the top-level keyword: `project NAME { ... }` ===
#
# One per project. Declares a prism over a `mirror.spec` file; the
# file's body is the four directives (source / legacy / target /
# settle_on). The compiler reads `mirror.spec` by evaluating it
# under @mirror/spec; no stand-alone parser. The file name matches
# the keyword (spec §2).
#
# === Alias-shim from `system` per two-tick discipline (Mara Round-3, 2026-07-20) ===
#
# Per Alex Round-3 spawn brief §Tier 1.4 verbatim: "shards/mirror/
# spec.mirror update: `system(name) -> prism` action-decl; `project`
# alias-shim for one release cycle."
#
# @mirror/spec/system (shards/mirror/spec/system.mirror this-tick)
# lands the SIBLING grammar `system @NAME { s1..s5 + feedback_loops
# + kintsugi_tooling }` block at compile-altitude altitude. Both
# grammars coexist during migration cycle:
#
#   TICK 1 (this tick):
#     - `project(name) -> prism` remains operational (unchanged surface;
#       this action-decl below)
#     - `system(name) -> prism` lands at @mirror/spec/system as sibling
#       grammar species
#     - Both keywords admitted in the tokenizer via shards/mirror/spec/
#       keywords.mirror (this-tick extension: `focus system`)
#
#   TICK 2 (forward-promised; next release cycle):
#     - Deprecate `project` grammar (deprecation warning at mosaic.focus
#       walk altitude)
#     - Update dogfood mirror.spec to use `system @mirror.spec { ... }`
#     - Update downstream consumer specs incrementally
#     - Retire `project` grammar (following release cycle)
#
# The dogfood update is FORWARD-PROMISED for TICK 2; NOT this tick per
# two-tick discipline (preserve consumer stability).
#
# The naming discipline (per Round-3 brief The one-sentence positioning):
# `system @X { ... }` is the compile-altitude landing of Beer's VSM;
# `project @X { ... }` is the legacy alias-shim during migration.
project(name) -> prism { \ }

# === the four directives inside a `project` block ===
#
# Per spec §§3-7. Each is a typed lambda (substrate's action form,
# per [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]]); the obligation
# block (\) is discharged by mosaic.focus when it walks the manifold.

# source ~d'...'
#
# One per project under `strict` (spec §3). Declares the canonical
# directory of substrate truth — the .mirror shards mosaic compiles.
# The compiler verifies the directory exists at compile time.
# Multiple `source` directives are a compile error under strict.
source(path: dir_ref) -> source_decl { \ }

# legacy ~d'...', ~d'...' { shrinkage_contract: ..., retirement_target: ... }
#
# Substrate floors with shrinkage contracts (spec §4). Lines under
# legacy MUST monotonically decrease as substrate-pull moves content
# into source/. `paths` is the list of legacy directories; each is a
# separate floor. `shrinkage_contract` is a @property predicate that
# must hold across builds. Mosaic tolerates these floors' existence
# but forbids growth; new shards cannot reference them.
legacy(paths: [dir_ref], shrinkage_contract: property) -> legacy_decl { \ }

# target NAME { ... }
#
# What gets built. Each target settles to au at one altitude
# (spec §5). Multiple targets are typical; mosaic walks the list,
# shifts each to its altitude, settles each independently, composes
# the transparency over all of them into the project's transparency.
# The body declares: name, altitude, emit, optional cli, optional
# needs. See sub-keywords below.
target(name) -> prism { \ }

# settle_on { <predicate>+ }
#
# Declares when mosaic considers the project settled (spec §7). Each
# predicate is an @property reference. Mosaic checks them after
# settlement; if all hold AND `total_transparency.weight == 0`, the
# build is settled (eⁿ⁺¹ < eⁿ at the spec altitude). Failed
# predicates become opacities for the next kintsugi iteration.
settle_on(predicates: [property]) -> settle_decl { \ }

# === sub-keywords inside a `target` block ===
#
# A target's interior consists of four field declarations. Per spec §5
# these are: name (str), altitude (ref(@meta/altitude)), emit
# (ref(@io) or grammar reference), and the optional cli (block)
# plus needs (option([ref])). Declared as typed lambdas so the
# obligation block (\) is discharged by mosaic when it resolves
# the target manifold.

# name "<artifact-name>" — the artifact name at the altitude.
name(value: str) -> name_decl { \ }

# altitude @<altitude-ref> — where the target settles.
altitude(value: ref) -> altitude_decl { \ }

# emit <ref|grammar> — which @io tool or grammar projection emits
# the artifact. Per spec §10.5: `emit cargo` resolves to a @io tool
# invocation through the altitude grammar; `emit yaml` resolves to
# a @facet/yaml grammar projection. Disambiguation is by type at
# the call site (open question — see spec §10.5).
emit(target: ref) -> emit_decl { \ }

# cli { ... } — the CLI surface, only meaningful when emit is a
# binary. The block uses @mirror/lens/cli (imported above); inside-target
# embedding per spec §6 and lens/cli.mirror's tightening: commands cannot
# escape the binary they belong to. Per the 2026-06-06 lens family
# migration: @mirror/cli is now @mirror/lens/cli; same shape, family
# placement clarified.
cli(body: cli) -> cli_decl { \ }

# needs [<target-ref>+] — DAG ordering between targets (spec §5).
# Optional. Mosaic resolves the DAG; settlement proceeds in
# topological order. When omitted, the target has no prerequisite
# settlements.
needs(targets: [ref]) -> needs_decl { \ }

# === tools { } block — @tool species pinning (forward-promise) ===
#
# Grammar extension parallel to `cli { }`, `pack { }`, `garden { }`,
# `kintsugi { }`. Substrate-decl'd at Mara's closure canonical spec
# `docs/specs/2026-07-18-the-compiler-in-one-sentence.md` §4 (the
# `tools { }` block); prose sketch this tick per §12.1 Deliverable A
# part 3 (Mara 2026-07-18); full grammar-mutation admission
# forward-promised to Reed post-landing Tick M3 territory (§12.1
# tick 3: "grammar-extension tick + species-decl tick + dispatch
# tick + dogfood tick = 4 ticks").
#
# Shape (per closure §4.1):
#
#   project mirror.spec {
#     ...
#     tools {
#       cargo { version "1.80" }        # via @tool/cargo species
#       git   { version "2.45" }        # via @tool/git species
#       nix   { version "2.24" }        # via @tool/nix species
#       ~bin'./scripts/mycheck.sh' { version "git+HEAD" }
#                                       # via ~bin sigil (Q2 answer;
#                                       # Alex 2026-07-18 direct-transcript)
#     }
#     ...
#   }
#
# Per closure §4.2: sits at the SAME altitude as `garden { }`. Both
# are @io-adjacent surface areas; both discharge via typed adapters
# (@io/git for garden; @tool(X, args) for tools); both admit empty-
# blocks as substrate-pull-honest explicit-emptiness. EMPTY
# `tools { }` is admissible (a project declaring "no external tool
# dependencies pinned"), though mirror itself ships cargo + git +
# nix as FLOOR species pins.
#
# Per closure §4.3: at dispatch time, `@roomba.walk` reads the
# tools{} block, resolves each pinned tool_id to its concrete version
# (via `@tool/<X>.version_of` or nix-pin via @tool/nix.resolve_pin),
# and biases Fate's next @tool(X, args) selection to the pinned set.
# Consumers CANNOT invoke an unpinned tool — the compiler's grammar
# refuses at settle-time. Consumers CAN escape via `~bin'<path>'` for
# tools without substrate-decl'd species.
#
# Forward-promised (Reed post-landing territory per closure §12.1):
#
#   tools(body: tool_pins_block) -> tool_pins_decl { \ }
#
# Where `tool_pins_block` is the substrate-decl'd carrier for the
# parsed block (list of tool_pin entries), and each `tool_pin` is a
# labeled(tool_id, tool_pin_body) carrier where tool_pin_body carries
# the `version` field + optional `args`, `env`, `working_dir`
# override fields.
#
# Companion species-decl `shards/mirror/tools.mirror` FORWARD-
# PROMISED (sibling of `shards/mirror/garden.mirror` +
# `shards/mirror/pack.mirror`; substrate-decls the block-body typed
# carrier + parse action + `tools_block_coherent` composed
# bilateral). Per closure §12.1: species-decl tick lands with
# grammar-extension tick.
#
# Companion keyword binding in `shards/mirror/spec/keywords.mirror`
# FORWARD-PROMISED: add `focus tools` (recursively-scanned brace
# block, parallel to `focus cli` + `settle settle_on`) at Reed
# post-landing Tick M3.

# check <action-ref> — names the @io action the target dispatches
# (the cargo subcommand at @facet/rust altitude). Optional; when
# omitted, the target dispatches the altitude's default (cargo check
# for @facet/rust today).
#
# The substrate-pull recognition (insight #43, 2026-06-09): the
# pre-commit chain (fmt / check / clippy / test / audit) IS five
# settlements on the build manifold, one per altitude action. Per
# shards/io/cargo.mirror these lift to `imperfect` through the same
# `cargo_exit_to_transparency` contract; the check directive is how
# mirror.spec names which one to run per target.
#
# Resolution: the `action` ref is looked up in the altitude's @io
# contract (today: shards/io/cargo.mirror). Substrate-pull-correct
# values for @facet/rust: check, test, build, fmt_check, clippy, audit,
# bench (per shards/io/cargo.mirror's declared actions).
#
# Per Seam Phase D `91e79c8` §7 Sub-arc 3a (RED `d25b91a`): `bench`
# joins the accepted `check` values to dispatch `cargo bench`, opening
# the perf-measurement floor for `target bench` blocks. Consumer:
# @mirror/bench (LANDED 2026-07-01 at `shards/mirror/bench.mirror`,
# 16.3KB) becomes the first harness wired into mirror.spec via the
# standard `emit cargo` / `check bench` dispatch path.
check(action: ref) -> check_decl { \ }

out @mirror/spec
out project
out source
out legacy
out target
out settle_on
out name
out altitude
out emit
out cli
out needs
out check
